NAME
     chroot - run a program with another root directory

SYNOPSIS
     chroot DIR [COMMAND [ARG...]]

DESCRIPTION
     chroot runs COMMAND (a shell by default) with DIR as /. It is
     root's alone, and it is not a container by itself: a process that
     keeps a descriptor to a directory outside can walk out of it, which
     is what pivot_root in a mount namespace is for.

SEE ALSO
     unshare(1), vmm(1)
